-- Directives that say something about the engine itself: the static type of an expression, the step budget, the evaluation counters, a peer's value fed in, and a restart on a store.

test the static type of an expression and what the checker finds
type Int(x) with x: Text = "Int|Error"
type Int(x) with x: Int = "Int"
findings Voice(kind: 1 + 'a') = 1

test a budget stops an evaluation that takes more steps than it
budget 3
eval 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 7 + 8 = error: budget
budget off
eval 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 7 + 8 = 36

test the engine counts the evaluations of a getter and a setter
PACK sa 1
StatsA.dbl getter: this.w * 2
StatsA.w on-setter copy:
  ALWAYS:
    this.z = this.w + 1
stats on
given StatsA:a {"w": 1}
write StatsA:a.w = 10
write StatsA:a.w = 11
stats getter StatsA.dbl calls >= 3
stats setter StatsA.w calls = 2
stats off

test a foreign read is pending until the peer says something
ns p1
PACK t 1
Light.c getter: why(membrane::Setting:t.val).cls
Light.v getter: membrane::Setting:t.val
given Light:a {}
reads Light:a.c = "Pending"
feed membrane::Setting:t = {"val": 4}
reads Light:a.v = 4
feed gone membrane::Setting:t
reads Light:a.c = "Absent"

test what was written is still there after a restart
store
PACK t 1
Note.twice getter: this.n * 2
given Note:a {"n": 1}
write Note:a.n = 2
restart
reads Note:a.n = 2
reads Note:a.twice = 4
